course: dictionary
lesson: 13138
title: Forcefully
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Forcefully is an adverb, so it tells you how someone does an action. It comes from force, which means strength or power. «She pushed the stuck door forcefully, and it swung open.» The word forcefully tells us she pushed with strength.
explain: Forcefully can also describe a strong, confident way of speaking or arguing that makes people listen. «He argued forcefully for a new park, and the council changed its mind.» Check your meaning by swapping in a simple word: he argued strongly and confidently. If it still makes sense, you have it.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Words like push, speak and argue often come before forcefully. The clues tell you the action was strong and determined, not gentle or quiet.
fact: Forcefully means with a lot of strength or power.
fact: It can also mean in a strong, confident way that makes people listen.
fact: «Push forcefully» means push with strength.
fact: Forcefully is often used with words like «speak», «argue» and «push».
fact: Forcefully tells the reader that an action was strong or determined.
exercise: «The wind blew forcefully against the tent all night.» How did the wind blow? | Quietly, like a whisper | *With great strength | Backwards only | Gently and slowly
exercise: «Maya spoke forcefully at the school meeting, and everyone listened.» What does forcefully suggest about Maya? | She was sleepy and bored | She was lost and afraid | *She was strong and confident | She was very small
exercise: «The coach told the team to run forcefully.» Find and copy the adverb in this sentence. | team | told | coach | *forcefully
test: «He knocked forcefully on the door.» What does forcefully mean here? | Softly and gently | *With strength and power | Very slowly | Without a sound
test: Which sentence shows someone arguing in a strong, confident way? | *«He argued forcefully, and the group listened.» | «It rained all afternoon.» | «She sat quietly and said nothing.» | «The cat slept on the mat.»
exam: «The referee blew the whistle forcefully, and the players stopped at once.» What does forcefully tell us? | It was done by accident | *It was done with strong power | It was done gently | It was done in the dark
